nters the battlefield, each opponent loses 1 life and you gain 1 life.\\nSacrifice a Food: Return Cauldron Familiar from your graveyard to the battlefield.', 'When Charming Prince enters the battlefield, choose one —\\n• Scry 2.\\n• You gain 3 life.\\n• Exile another target creature you own. Return it to the battlefield under your control at the beginning of the next end step.', 'When Chittering Witch enters the battlefield, create a number of 1/1 black Rat creature tokens equal to the number of opponents you have.\\n{1}{B}, Sacrifice a creature: Target creature gets -2/-2 until end of turn.', 'When Corridor Monitor enters the battlefield, untap target artifact or creature you control.', 'When Enchanted Carriage enters the battlefield, create two 1/1 white Mouse creature tokens.\\nCrew 2 (Tap any number of creatures you control with total power 2 or more: This Vehicle becomes an artifact creature until end of turn.)', 'When Gadwick, the Wizened enters the battlefield, draw X cards.\\nWhenever you cast a blue spell, tap target nonland permanent an opponent controls.', 'When Glass Casket enters the battlefield, exile target creature an opponent controls with mana value 3 or less until Glass Casket leaves the battlefield.', 'When Golden Egg enters the battlefield, draw a card.\\n{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Golden Egg: Add one mana of any color.\\n{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Golden Egg: You gain 3 life.', 'When Happily Ever After enters the battlefield, each player gains 5 life and draws a card.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, if there are five colors among permanents you control, there are six or more card types among permanents you control and/or cards in your graveyard, and your life total is greater than or equal to your starting life total, you win the game.', 'When Inquisitive Puppet enters the battlefield, scry 1.\\nExile Inquisitive Puppet: Create a 1/1 white Human creature token.', 'When Lost Legion enters the battlefield, scry 2. (Look at the top two cards of your library, then put any number of them on the bottom of your library and the rest on top in any order.)', "When Moonlit Scavengers enters the battlefield, if you control an artifact or enchantment, return target creature an opponent controls to its owner's hand.", 'When Overwhelmed Apprentice enters the battlefield, each opponent mills two cards. Then you scry 2. (Look at the top two cards of your library, then put any number of them on the bottom of your library and the rest on top in any order.)', 'When Prophet of the Peak enters the battlefield, scry 2. (Look at the top two cards of your library, then put any number of them on the bottom of your library and the rest on top in any order.)', 'When Rosethorn Halberd enters the battlefield, attach it to target non-Human creature you control.\\nEquipped creature gets +2/+1.\\nEquip {5} ({5}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)', "When Rowan's Stalwarts enters the battlefield, you may search your library and/or graveyard for a card named Rowan, Fearless Sparkmage, reveal it, and put it into your hand. If you search your library this way, shuffle.", 'When Tempting Witch enters the battlefield, create a Food token. (It\'s an artifact with "{2}, {T}, Sacrifice this artifact: You gain 3 life.")\\n{2}, {T}, Sacrifice a Food: Target player loses 3 life.', 'When Trail of Crumbs enters the battlefield, create a Food token. (It\'s an artifact with "{2}, {T}, Sacrifice this artifact: You gain 3 life.")\\nWhenever you sacrifice a Food, you may pay {1}. If you do, look at the top two cards of your library. You may reveal a permanent card from among them and put it into your hand. Put the rest on the bottom of your library in any order.', 'When Venerable Knight dies, put a +1/+1 counter on target Knight you control.', 'When Wicked Guardian enters the battlefield, you may have it deal 2 damage to another creature you control. If you do, draw a card.', "When Wicked Wolf enters the battlefield, it fights up to one target creature you don't control.\\nSacrifice a Food: Put a +1/+1 counter on Wicked Wolf. It gains indestructible until end of turn. Tap it.", 'When Witching Well enters the battlefield, scry 2. (Look at the top two cards of your library, then put any number of them on the bottom of your library and the rest on top in any order.)\\n{3}{U}, Sacrifice Witching Well: Draw two cards.', "When you cast this spell from your hand, copy it if you control an artifact, then copy it if you control an enchantment. You may choose new targets for the copies.\\nReturn target nonland permanent to its owner's hand. You create a 2/2 white Knight creature token with vigilance.", 'Whenever Ayara, First of Locthwain or another black creature enters the battlefield under your control, each opponent loses 1 life and you gain 1 life.\\n{T}, Sacrifice another black creature: Draw a card.', "Whenever Bonecrusher Giant becomes the target of a spell, Bonecrusher Giant deals 2 damage to that spell's controller.", 'Whenever Flaxen Intruder deals combat damage to a player, you may sacrifice it. When you do, destroy target artifact or enchantment.', "Whenever Mistford River Turtle attacks, another target attacking non-Human creature can't be blocked this turn.", "Whenever Ogre Errant attacks, another target attacking Knight gains menace until end of turn. (It can't be blocked except by two or more creatures.)", "Whenever Queen of Ice deals combat damage to a creature, tap that creature. It doesn't untap during its controller's next untap step.", 'Whenever Reaper of Night attacks, if defending player has two or fewer cards in hand, it gains flying until end of turn.', 'Whenever Redcap Raiders attacks, you may tap an untapped non-Human creature you control. If you do, Redcap Raiders gets +1/+1 and gains trample until end of turn.', 'Whenever Sage of the Falls or another non-Human creature enters the battlefield under your control, you may draw a card. If you do, discard a card.', 'Whenever Savvy Hunter attacks or blocks, create a Food token. (It\'s an artifact with "{2}, {T}, Sacrifice this artifact: You gain 3 life.")\\nSacrifice two Foods: Draw a card.', 'Whenever Skullknocker Ogre deals damage to an opponent, that player discards a card at random. If the player does, they draw a card.', 'Whenever Syr Carah, the Bold or an instant or sorcery spell you control deals damage to a player, exile the top card of your library. You may play that card this turn.\\n{T}: Syr Carah deals 1 damage to any target.', "Whenever Syr Faren, the Hengehammer attacks, another target attacking creature gets +X/+X until end of turn, where X is Syr Faren's power.", 'Whenever Wildwood Tracker attacks or blocks, if you control another non-Human creature, Wildwood Tracker gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', "Whenever a Knight you control attacks, each opponent loses 1 life and you gain 1 life.\\n{6}{W}{B}, Sacrifice Knights' Charge: Return all Knight creature cards from your graveyard to the battlefield.", "Whenever a creature attacks you or a planeswalker you control, that creature's controller loses 1 life and you gain 1 life.", 'Whenever another creature dies, or a creature card is put into a graveyard from anywhere other than the battlefield, or a creature card leaves your graveyard, Syr Konrad, the Grim deals 1 damage to each opponent.\\n{1}{B}: Each player mills a card. (They each put the top card of their library into their graveyard.)', 'Whenever one or more non-Human creatures you control deal combat damage to a player, draw a card.', 'Whenever you cast a Knight spell, create a 1/1 white Human creature token.', "Whenever you cast a creature spell that has an Adventure, Garenbrig Squire gets +1/+1 until end of turn. (It doesn't need to have gone on the adventure first.)", "Whenever you cast a creature spell that has an Adventure, draw a card. (It doesn't need to have gone on the adventure first.)", "Whenever you cast a creature spell that has an Adventure, put a +1/+1 counter on Wandermare. (It doesn't need to have gone on the adventure first.)", 'Whenever you cast a spell with mana value 5 or greater, draw a card.', 'Whenever you cast an Adventure instant or sorcery spell, copy it. You may choose new targets for the copy.', 'Whenever you draw your second card each turn, Bloodhaze Wolverine gets +1/+1 and gains first strike until end of turn.', 'Whenever you draw your second card each turn, Irencrag Pyromancer deals 3 damage to any target.', 'Whenever you draw your second card each turn, create a 1/1 blue Faerie creature token with flying.\\n{4}{U}{R}: Draw a card, then discard a card.', 'Whenever you draw your second card each turn, create two 1/1 black Rat creature tokens.', "Whenever you sacrifice another permanent, you may pay {3}. If you do, create a token that's a copy of Sorcerer's Broom.", 'Wind-Scarred Crag enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Wind-Scarred Crag enters the battlefield, you gain 1 life.\\n{T}: Add {R} or {W}.', 'Wishclaw Talisman enters the battlefield with three wish counters on it.\\n{1}, {T}, Remove a wish counter from Wishclaw Talisman: Search your library for a card, put it into your hand, then shuffle. An opponent gains control of Wishclaw Talisman. Activate only during your turn.', "Yorvo, Lord of Garenbrig enters the battlefield with four +1/+1 counters on it.\\nWhenever another green creature enters the battlefield under your control, put a +1/+1 counter on Yorvo. Then if that creature's power is greater than Yorvo's power, put another +1/+1 counter on Yorvo.", 'You can cast spells only during your turn and you can cast no more than two spells each turn.\\nYou may cast spells with mana value less than or equal to the number of lands you control without paying their mana costs.', 'You draw a card and you lose 1 life. (Then exile this card. You may cast the creature later from exile.)', 'You gain X life and each opponent loses X life, where X is the number of Knights you control.', 'You may discard a card. If you do, draw a card. (Then exile this card. You may cast the creature later from exile.)', 'You may have Mirrormade enter the battlefield as a copy of any artifact or enchantment on the battlefield.', 'You may reveal a noncreature card you own from outside the game and put it into your hand.', 'You may sacrifice a Food. If you do, target creature gets +5/+5 until end of turn. Otherwise, that creature gets +3/+3 until end of turn.', 'You may sacrifice two Foods. If you do, create a 7/7 green Giant creature token. Otherwise, create three Food tokens. (They\'re artifacts with "{2}, {T}, Sacrifice this artifact: You gain 3 life.")', '[+1]: Draw a card, then discard a card.\\n[+1]: Target creature gets +2/+0 and gains first strike and trample until end of turn.\\n[−8]: Draw four cards. When you do, The Royal Scions deals damage to any target equal to the number of cards in your hand.', '[+1]: Put two +1/+1 counters on up to one target creature you control.\\n[0]: Until end of turn, Oko, the Trickster becomes a copy of target creature you control. Prevent all damage that would be dealt to him this turn.\\n[−7]: Until end of turn, each creature you control has base power and toughness 10/10 and gains trample.', "[+1]: Up to one target creature gets +3/+0 and gains first strike until end of turn.\\n[−2]: Rowan, Fearless Sparkmage deals 1 damage to each of up to two target creatures. Those creatures can't block this turn.\\n[−9]: Gain control of all creatures until end of turn. Untap them. They gain haste until end of turn.", '[+2]: Create a Food token. (It\'s an artifact with "{2}, {T}, Sacrifice this artifact: You gain 3 life.")\\n[+1]: Target artifact or creature loses all abilities and becomes a green Elk creature with base power and toughness 3/3.\\n[−5]: Exchange control of target artifact or creature you control and target creature an opponent controls with power 3 or less.', '[0]: Create two 2/2 black and green Wolf creature tokens with "When this creature dies, put a loyalty counter on each Garruk you control."\\n[−3]: Destroy target creature. Draw a card.\\n[−6]: You get an emblem with "Creatures you control get +3/+3 and have trample."', '{1}{R}: Weaselback Redcap gets +2/+0 until end of turn.', '{1}{W}, {T}: Tap target creature.', '{2}, Sacrifice an artifact or another creature: Put a +1/+1 counter on Malevolent Noble.', '{2}{R}, Discard a card: Draw a card.', '{3}, {T}, Sacrifice Scalding Cauldron: It deals 3 damage to target creature.', '{3}: Jousting Dummy gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', '{4}: Locthwain Gargoyle gets +2/+0 and gains flying until end of turn.', '{8}: Bramblefort Fink has base power and toughness 10/10 until end of turn. Activate only if you control an Oko planeswalker.', "{R}: All creatures gain trample and haste until end of turn.\\n{1}{G}: Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature.\\n{2}{W}: Target player gains 5 life.\\n{3}{U}: Target player draws a card.\\n{4}{B}: Put target creature card from a graveyard onto the battlefield under its owner's control.", '{T}, Sacrifice Fabled Passage: Search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle. Then if you control four or more lands, untap that land.', '{T}, Sacrifice a creature: Create a Food token. If the sacrificed creature\'s toughness was 4 or greater, create two Food tokens instead. (They\'re artifacts with "{2}, {T}, Sacrifice this artifact: You gain 3 life.")', "{T}: Add one mana of any color in your commander's color identity.", '{T}: Add one mana of any color.', '{T}: Add one mana of any color.\\n{5}, {T}: Tap target creature.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {R}, {W}, or {B}. Spend this mana only to cast a Knight or Equipment spell.', '{T}: Add {U}.\\n{2}{U}: Put an hour counter on Midnight Clock.\\nAt the beginning of each upkeep, put an hour counter on Midnight Clock.\\nWhen the twelfth hour counter is put on Midnight Clock, shuffle your hand and graveyard into your library, then draw seven cards. Exile Midnight Clock.', '{T}: Creatures you control get +1/+1 until end of turn.', '{W/B}{W/B}: Resolute Rider gains lifelink until end of turn.\\n{W/B}{W/B}{W/B}: Resolute Rider gains indestructible until end of turn. (Damage and effects that say "destroy" don\'t destroy it.)']
flavor: ['"A good steed will carry you home. A great steed will carry you to glory."\\n—Syr Alin, the Lion\'s Claw', '"A keen eye and steady hand are essential for defeating most foes, including hunger."\\n—Syr Grenphire, knight of Garenbrig', '"A traditional lance is fine for the Burning Yard, but in the wilds you need a nastier bite."\\n—Kenver, Embereth weaponsmith', '"Accursed scarecrow! Sending folk in every direction is the same as sending them nowhere at all."\\n—Corliss the Wanderer', '"After the death of her mother, Cassia found that things that appear fragile can be very strong indeed."\\n—*Beyond the Great Henge*', '"Another angry mob? When will they learn to leave me be?"\\n—Terryn, Edgewall outcast', '"Approach my tower on bended knee or depart from it as ash upon the wind."\\n—Gadwick, the Wizened', '"As she reached the pinnacle, lightning flashed and her eyes blazed with newfound power."\\n—*Legend of the Gilded Knights*', '"As the traitor hurried across the courtyard, its eyes snapped open. It was time to pay the queen a visit."\\n—*Beyond the Great Henge*', '"At least up here I have some peace and quiet."', '"Be careful, dear. Some people deserve their curses."\\n—Marawen, barrow witch', '"Build a moat. If we\'re lucky, it can\'t swim."\\n—Syr Branigan, knight of Ardenvale', '"Buying old, worn out junk. Selling marvels of real value."', '"Buying old, worn-out junk. Selling marvels of real value."', '"By hoof, wing, or paw. For the realm!"\\n—Syr Gwyn, Hero of Ashvale', '"Courage is the only shield I need."', '"Does it matter what it is? Take it and be grateful!"', '"Don\'t let it fool you. Many of us got our first scars from Syr Nobody."\\n—Syr Layne, knight of Embereth', '"Duty and honor are reasons enough, but beating you will also be a pleasure."', '"Even as we mourn the last, we look to the next with joy. Hopefully, my new suitor will bring the Cauldron home."\\n—Ayara, First of Locthwain', '"Even when hope is but a small flame fighting the night, I will serve the absent king."', '"Fear not what\'s under the bed. The toys are watching."\\n—*Beyond the Great Henge*', '"Fear of fire is a sensible instinct. If I were you, I\'d be terrified."', '"Find him a weapon as big as his dreams."\\n—Yorvo, lord of Garenbrig', '"For every scar I\'ve received, I\'ve given ten back."', '"Gather round and tell me all from the courts and castles."', '"He has strength and courage—just way, way too much of both."\\n—Syr Faren, the Hengehammer', '"Headed to the wilds? Beware the dead riders who serve the Shadow Queen."\\n—Scalan, Edgewall innkeeper', '"Hone the knife and mourn the least. Three chimes to sound the sweet, grim feast."\\n—Barrow witch incantation', '"Humans are so forgetful. Every page I steal becomes a secret they can\'t remember."', '"I admire their courage as much as I despise their savagery."\\n—Syr Carah, the Bold', '"I agreed to light his way as long as he always had my back."\\n—Squill, Mistford pixie', '"I fight for my daughter, who may not set foot on a battlefield for many years. Remember who you fight for."', '"I will find the king if I have to ride from summer to winter and back again."', '"I would rather cast myself into the abyss than let my blood stain the cap of those monsters."\\n—Syr Alin, the Lion\'s Claw', '"I wrote these tales with a quill made from a griffin\'s feather. And the winning of that feather is quite a tale itself."\\n—Chulane, Teller of Tales', '"If it has ears, it will dance to my tune."', '"If we didn\'t guard our secrets, they wouldn\'t remain secrets for long."\\n—Gadwick, the Wizened', '"If you\'re as loyal as you claim, now is the time to show it."\\n—Queen Linden of Ardenvale', '"If you\'re in our home, we expect you to mind your manners."', '"Imagine having your skeleton extracted through your ear, one bone at a time."\\n—Corliss the Wanderer', '"In the wilds, your true training will begin."\\n—Syr Alin, the Lion\'s Claw', '"Into amethyst, I pour\\nEnvy\'s shadow, sorrow\'s gleam.\\nLure the one whose scorn I bore\\nThat I may hear one final scream."\\n—Barrow witch incantation', '"It wandered slowly across the landscape, calling out in its lonely voice, but no other castles answered its cries."\\n—*Beyond the Great Henge*', '"It\'s a witch\'s trick, this cauldron full of pain. I wouldn\'t dump it on any but the wicked."', '"It\'s gingerbread, like Mother makes. What is there to be afraid of?"', '"Just tell us how many you want and get out of the way."', '"Let\'s begin this conversation again, and this time you will only listen."', '"Life is a tournament that rewards the bold."\\n—Syr Layne, knight of Embereth', '"Long after the magic wore off, the mice still dreamed of glorious galloping."\\n—*Tales of the Fae*', '"Lord Rankle will see you now—all he asks is a small token of tribute."', '"May this blade guide you on your great journey, as it did me on mine."', '"Murder clad in crimson beauty,\\nAn end to life and love and duty."\\n—Barrow witch incantation', '"My advisors recommend I let them eat you."\\n—Oko', '"My quest? Why, to marry Ayara. Or die trying."', '"My secret ingredient? Well, I can\'t tell you that. But here\'s a hint. It\'s not love."', '"Old battlefields make great gardens. So rich from the blood of the fallen."', '"Only the lion knows more stories than I do."\\n—Chulane, Teller of Tales', '"Poor, lost mage. Your feet are on land, yet you\'re in over your head, aren\'t you?"', '"Rankle\'s pranks are child\'s play. My games will topple kingdoms."', '"Remember all the great heroes who were careful and never did anything risky? Me neither."\\n—Syr Carah, the Bold', '"Respect the wilds? Certainly. Fear them? No."', '"Reynald wished for an army to sweep away his enemies. The fae king smiled."\\n—*Beyond the Great Henge*', '"Right now you are a feeble stick, but I will help you grow some rings."', '"Share your darkest secret and the Mirror will reveal your soul\'s essence."\\n—Ceri, royal mirrorkeeper', '"Some are born to greatness. You were born to scrub greatness\'s floors."', '"Someone knows where the king is. They can\'t expect to keep it a secret from us."', '"Sometimes the hardest choice is between two wonders."\\n—Gadwick, the Wizened', '"Taste the sweetness, breath for breath. Keep the balance, death for death."\\n—Barrow witch incantation', '"The Northern Beacon flared, and even before the drawbridge finished its descent, the knights charged out."\\n—*Legend of the Gilded Knights*', '"The curse is broken."', '"The deal was struck and the favor had been done. And so, under the cover of night, the debt was paid."\\n—*Tales of the Fae*', '"The faerie plucked an acorn off the ground. One knight\'s quest was about to come to a bitter end."\\n—*Tales of the Fae*', '"The gleam of rubies and my brothers and sisters by my side . . . what more could I want?"\\n—Brognold the Third', '"The king would die for the realm. I would not hesitate to do the same for him."', '"The monster was gaining on them. Twice it had found them. There was only one place left to hide."\\n—*Tales of the Fae*', '"The realm must never yield to the chaos of the wilds."', '"The strings were gone, but he still felt the pull of invisible forces tugging at his mind."\\n—*Beyond the Great Henge*', '"The white fox grinned. \'How about a bet, dragon? If I win, the skies are mine.\' After he stopped laughing, the dragon agreed."\\n—*Tales of the Fae*', '"The young squire gripped her sword as the clanking stranger emerged. It was no knight that had come to challenge her."\\n—*Beyond the Great Henge*', '"They have forsaken their vows. The edict of the Circle demands their voices be silenced."\\n—Syr Tasdale, knight of Ardenvale', '"This one was wearing shoes made of glass. She\'ll be no ordinary prey."', '"This sword is Sunrise. The other is Dawn. They mark the beginning of my days but the end of yours."', '"Though long forgotten, the wheel continued to turn, spinning fate from a dusty attic."\\n—*Beyond the Great Henge*', '"To the king, to the Circle, and to the realm! And to not dying."', '"Until my last breath, I will defend the realm."', '"Virtue is virtue, whatever the heart that nurtures it."\\n—Malacan, Vantress exile', '"Warmth. Safety. A fully-stocked larder. You\'ll find nothing like Edgewall Keep in the wilds, I promise you that!"', '"We fight with valor in our hearts and fire in our veins!"', '"What good is loyalty to the crown if we are not also in service to those less fortunate? I fight for all of us."', '"What size advantage? They never even see me coming."', '"With the drum of hooves and a flash of blades, the monster\'s terrifying roar changed to a cry of fear."\\n—*Legend of the Gilded Knights*', '"Words are pointless. It\'s what you do with your hammer that counts."', '"You think these walls will protect you?\\nMy, you have a dim view of the power of the wilds."\\n—Marawen, barrow witch', '2018 World Champion Javier Dominguez', '2018 World Champion Javier Domínguez', "A dwarf's grudge runs deeper than the mountains' roots.", "A faerie's glee at her trove quickly fades to contentment, then to boredom, then to an urge to steal more.", 'A true puppet master has no need for strings.', "After years of taunts and aerial assaults from Rankle's minions, the witches of Maraleaf Forest acquired new familiars.", 'As the blaze raced toward her, Syr Ameril closed her eyes and pictured Castle Ardenvale so her last thoughts would be of home.', 'Ask a merfolk even a simple question and the answer is a journey far beyond the known.', 'At first, Syr Fenwick scoffed when he saw his opponents for the final match.', "At the market, no one heeded Hilda's frantic mooing. The fae curse was turning out even worse than she had feared.", 'Beacons along the borderlands are lit at any incursion from the wilds.', 'Cast out of Garenbrig for his crimes, Ennor turned to fae magic to fashion the perfect weapon for his revenge.', 'Castle Vantress has no locks on its doors, but interlopers rarely make it past the foyer.', 'Countless knights of Garenbrig owe their lives to his peerless craftsmanship.', "Denizens of the wilds don't always seek to harm intruders. Sometimes they simply misplace them.", "Despite its ferocity, its favor can be won with a gift of something it's never seen before.", 'Even death cannot diminish the persistence of the knights of Locthwain.', 'Every Ardenvale aspirant must step through the flame. Their honor determines whether they burn or shine.', "Every day the cat returns to kill the same mouse, which sinks again into the cauldron's brew.", "Every hero's journey starts somewhere.", 'Everything that inhabits Garenbrig is affected by the wild magic flowing through the Great Henge.', "Fate will decide whether it's a bed or a tomb.", 'First among equals.', "For good or ill, most fae can't resist meddling in the adventures of any knight they meet.", 'From here, the path to anywhere may be found.', 'Giants believe that tossing redcaps at knights is the best way to deal with both.', 'He ate them out of house and home and shed and barn and flock and herd.', 'He endured the white-hot blaze of the Circle and the sweltering heat of the Irencrag, and he emerged victorious.', "He has slain a dozen witches, luring each with a promise of fresh children's bones.", 'He realized a bit late that he was supposed to *plant* the magic beans.', 'His mind chose solitude, but his heart disagreed.', 'His name is spoken only in whispers—but he hears just the same.', 'His sword sounded like a silver chime on the glass jar, and the sprite laughed with delight.', "History may be written by the triumphant, but it's often rewritten by the troublesome.", 'In a castle that prizes loyalty above all, the bond between knight and griffin is unmatched.', 'In the end, death usually has its way.', 'In the wilds, the ravens steal far more than baubles.', 'It emerged from the coldest depths of Lochmere only to face the fires of Irencrag.', 'It frequently predicts imminent death by devouring.', 'It started as a mere drop of water. The Magic Mirror crystallized it into much more.', 'It was built by the Witch of Lochmere. Most of the wishes it grants are its own.', 'It will come to the defense of all wild things, from the shivering wren to the towering giant.', 'Its wide-reaching roots draw more than water.', "Knights kept returning from Ogre's Pass wearing nothing but bruises, so they decided to just pretend it was on their side.", 'Knights who excel in tournaments sometimes underestimate threats beyond the realm.', 'Locthwain knights take pride in being the last ones standing in a fight or on a dance floor.', 'Many an ancient treasure has been reduced to jagged caltrops by its snapping jaws.', 'Many tales of redcap terror begin with two simple things: bloodlust and stolen steel.', 'Merfolk curiosity usually has dire consequences, but rarely for the merfolk.', 'Mourning shifts seamlessly to celebration as she chooses her next suitor.', 'Neither hostile nor friendly, pixies flit through the forest seeking the treasures of the wilds.', "No matter the cruelty of Oko's jokes, he's always guaranteed the sycophant's laughter.", "No one is so lost that a faerie can't find them.", 'No one knows when the tournament began. All they know is that it will never end.', 'No weapon stays on the rack for long in the Burning Yard.', 'None of the other villagers dare venture into the wilds, so she feeds the whole hamlet herself.', 'Not all heroes carry swords.', 'Not every tale ends in glory.', 'Nothing remains of his foes but the gripping story of their downfall.', 'Rowan and Will exchanged a baffled glance. Could the stag in the vision lead them to their father?', 'She yearned to walk on dry land so she might take her vengeance there.', "Some are annoyed by the constant ticking as they clean the cobbles, but to the castle custodians, there's no sweeter sound.", "Sometimes a gentle slipper can travel where an armored boot's been denied.", 'Squires throughout the realm aspire to her mix of panache and martial prowess.', 'Syr Branigan always remembered to kiss his good luck charm, having lost his foot to wolverines the last time he forgot.', 'Syr Damon looked at the dragon and saw the faces of every innocent it had devoured. Suddenly, his sword blazed like the sun.', 'Syr Tasdale declared that he never wanted to see the witch Ygretta again. Her familiars quickly granted his request.', 'Tempered by fire and united in virtue, the knights of Ardenvale fight with a single, unbreakable will.', 'That gnat was still hovering by the venison, and now both looked delicious.', 'The Blacklances travel deep into the wilds, sometimes for years at a time, in search of the lost Cauldron of Eternity.', 'The boundary between real and imaginary is as thin as the page, and just as easily torn.', "The dragon had a lot of things going through his mind that day. He didn't expect a sword to be one of them.", 'The elves remember every secret path from the days when they ruled the realm.', 'The fae raised the turtle from a tiny hatchling. They taught it whom to ferry—and whom to drown.', "The giant had heard of locks, but he had yet to discover a door he couldn't open.", "The greatest challenge isn't the stifling heat but the crushing weight of those who failed before.", "The guards kindled the hearth and locked the door to Ellwen's chamber. By morning, the fire was out and Ellwen was gone.", 'The hex swept through the village, its citizens falling one by one.', 'The indigo dragon gladly traded a bit of its hoard for everlasting moonlight.', 'The keen-eyed guardians of Ardenvale are ever on alert.', 'The middle blade was just right.', 'The ogre crashed through the massive door. The winged folios scattered like frightened birds.', 'The purest virtue burns brighter than the sun and hotter than dragonfire.', 'The throng flitted from castle to castle, leaving a trail of star-crossed love, damaging rumors, and missing heirlooms in their wake.', 'The unlabeled vial was not vanilla extract after all.', 'The wafting smells are both scrumptious and suspicious.', 'They both hunger for battle.', 'They comb the shallows of Lochmere for relics of a bygone era. And if they happen upon a lone traveler, all the better.', 'They function as everything from assassins to jesters in the name of their fae king.', 'They look tasty, but best to plant them.', 'Those who say you only live once have never been touched by the Cauldron of Eternity.', 'Transformed at his own wedding, he promptly ate the banquet, the gifts, and the guests.', 'While humans hear only a deafening roar, the fae hear music of breathtaking beauty.', 'While the realm has laws, in the wilds there are other ways of balancing power.', "Without Ardenvale's loyalty, the realm would greedily devour itself.", "Without Embereth's courage, the realm would falter and fall.", "Without Garenbrig's strength, the realm would succumb to the wilds.", "Without Locthwain's persistence, the realm would stagnate and die.", "Without Vantress's knowledge, the realm would lose itself in darkness."]
